diff --git a/docs/annotation-surfaces.md b/docs/annotation-surfaces.md
index 8012bb4..1e308aa 100644
--- a/docs/annotation-surfaces.md
+++ b/docs/annotation-surfaces.md
@@ -26,9 +26,18 @@ Optional methods:
 
 - `begin()` / `finish()`: acquire/release annotation resources. `finish` must be
   safe after the viewer closes.
-- `turn(direction, done)`: navigate, then call `done(surface)` once the new
+- `turn(direction, done, frame)`: navigate, then call `done(surface)` once the new
   surface and its geometry are ready. The old ink is saved before this call.
   Navigation can be asynchronous. A drawing canvas stays modal over its viewer.
+  The optional `frame(surface)` callback requests a live editor repaint after
+  each camera update. The editor snapshots the surface with saved ink during
+  movement, blocks editing, and reloads editable ops at completion. Late
+  completions after editor closure/replacement are ignored. Providers accepting
+  only the original two arguments remain compatible.
+- `readingDirection()`: `"rtl"` or `"ltr"`. Physical arrows and unbound navigation
+  swipes follow this direction. Semantic next/previous actions remain logical
+  forward/backward. Without this method the normal reader's inverse-reading-order
+  setting is used. No provider or plugin-specific identifiers are needed.
 - `mapPath(points, to_page, page)`: map a flat x/y path, inserting vertices at
   layout discontinuities. Needed when an affine transform alone is insufficient.
 - `isAffine()`: false when primitive shape outlines need path mapping.
